      "_id": "QoHMU4cNgLseZgOW",
      "name": "Gills",
      "type": "physicalTech",
      "system": {
        "description": "<p>The morph&rsquo;s lung tissue is adapted to function as gills, allowing you to breathe both air and water, as long as the water is not toxic or too stagnant. Water you breathe in through the gills is expelled through slits just underneath your lowest pair of ribs that seal when you are not underwater.</p>",
